1
00:00:27,818 --> 00:00:29,320
Nice of you to show up, Pokey.

2
00:00:29,612 --> 00:00:31,822
Yeah, sorry I'm late.
Bad traffic on the 50.

3
00:00:31,989 --> 00:00:34,784
Looks like the coroner's finishing up.
Talk to him, see what he's got.

4
00:00:35,535 --> 00:00:37,703
- Hey, traffic got lipstick on you.
- What? Where?

5
00:00:38,371 --> 00:00:40,540
Hope she gave you breakfast.
Forensics ate all the bagels.

6
00:00:41,582 --> 00:00:43,584
Late and later.
What's your excuse?

7
00:00:43,751 --> 00:00:45,002
It's all a journey, Lisbon.

8
00:00:45,753 --> 00:00:47,672
She washed up here
sometime last night.

9
00:00:47,797 --> 00:00:49,966
A jogger found her this morning
called it in.

10
00:00:50,383 --> 00:00:52,760
The only identifiable mark
is that tattoo.

11
00:00:54,095 --> 00:00:56,097
Coroner says she was strangled
before she hit the water.

12
00:00:56,514 --> 00:00:59,225
Some tissue under her fingernails.
Might've scratched the killer.

13
00:00:59,684 --> 00:01:01,352
No sign of sexual assault.

14
00:01:03,229 --> 00:01:04,272
- Lisbon.
- Yeah?

15
00:01:04,438 --> 00:01:06,274
- Check between her toes.
- Why?

16
00:01:06,566 --> 00:01:07,858
Because I don't really want to.

17
00:01:10,778 --> 00:01:12,405
- Needle marks.
- She was an addict?

18
00:01:13,114 --> 00:01:14,699
Manicure but no pedicure.

19
00:01:15,032 --> 00:01:16,534
Didn't want people
to see her feet.

20
00:01:17,410 --> 00:01:20,413
The track marks don't seem fresh.
Maybe she got clean.

21
00:01:20,871 --> 00:01:22,748
As soon as the M.E. identifies her

22
00:01:22,873 --> 00:01:25,084
I want you to go and see
if she has any drug arrests

23
00:01:25,209 --> 00:01:27,837
- and check out the local rehab centers.
- Yeah, you got it.

24
00:01:32,425 --> 00:01:33,467
- Yeah?
- "Mr. Jane"

25
00:01:33,593 --> 00:01:35,970
"this is Agent Vint Molinari,
Missing Persons."

26
00:01:36,095 --> 00:01:37,972
"I'm on the Kristina Frye case."

27
00:01:38,556 --> 00:01:42,018
An old client of Frye's was listening
to some psychic call-in show

28
00:01:42,143 --> 00:01:43,436
on the radio the other day

29
00:01:43,644 --> 00:01:45,605
heard somebody she swears
was Kristina.

30
00:01:46,397 --> 00:01:47,982
"We've got a recording
of the show."

31
00:01:48,816 --> 00:01:51,569
Can you tell me
if this is her voice?

32
00:01:51,986 --> 00:01:54,572
"I spoke to the last
caller's late mother Susan."

33
00:01:54,697 --> 00:01:55,865
"She told me she's happy"

34
00:01:56,324 --> 00:01:59,660
"and wants her daughter to know
how proud of her she is."

35
00:02:00,411 --> 00:02:02,622
It's her.
Did you trace the call?

36
00:02:02,747 --> 00:02:04,999
Comes from a landline
house on Delmore Road

37
00:02:05,291 --> 00:02:06,459
north of Fremont Landing.

38
00:02:07,627 --> 00:02:09,295
"I'll let you know
if we find anything there."

39
00:02:33,069 --> 00:02:35,112
Jane. How you doing?

40
00:03:38,924 --> 00:03:39,967
Blood on the wall--

41
00:03:40,509 --> 00:03:43,095
DNA analysis says
it's Frye's.

42
00:03:44,596 --> 00:03:47,766
{\an8}And the house was clean.
No prints or trace evidence of any kind.

43
00:03:48,434 --> 00:03:50,269
{\an8}No sign of a body or a grave.

44
00:03:50,769 --> 00:03:54,148
{\an8}She's alive. If he killed her,
he would've left her body out on display.

45
00:03:54,606 --> 00:03:57,735
{\an8}Vint, it looks like this is more than just
a missing persons case to me.

46
00:03:58,152 --> 00:04:01,321
{\an8}I'm gonna talk to the head of the division
and ask him to hand the case over to us.

47
00:04:01,905 --> 00:04:04,074
{\an8}Why? Because it's Red John
and you're the Red John guys?

48
00:04:05,200 --> 00:04:06,285
{\an8}I've read his file, too.

49
00:04:07,786 --> 00:04:09,288
Frye's been missing
for four months.

50
00:04:09,788 --> 00:04:12,458
{\an8}Red John never kept a victim alive
for more than a few days.

51
00:04:12,708 --> 00:04:14,626
{\an8}He never left
a-a clue on the scene

52
00:04:14,752 --> 00:04:16,503
except for the--the painted face.

53
00:04:17,171 --> 00:04:19,298
And that call Frye made--
that's hardly a cry for help.

54
00:04:19,506 --> 00:04:20,549
What's your point?

55
00:04:20,674 --> 00:04:22,551
{\an8}Well, who knows if Red John
had anything to do with this?

56
00:04:23,093 --> 00:04:25,471
{\an8}As far as I know
Frye painted the face herself.

57
00:04:25,846 --> 00:04:27,055
Why would she do that?

58
00:04:29,099 --> 00:04:30,893
{\an8}Well, the woman thinks
she talks to the dead.

59
00:04:31,685 --> 00:04:33,479
She's half a nutcase
walking out the door.

60
00:04:33,645 --> 00:04:35,773
{\an8}Lisbon, I-I agree
with Agent Molinari.

61
00:04:36,315 --> 00:04:38,484
{\an8}Kristina's case should remain
in his capable hands.

62
00:04:38,609 --> 00:04:40,444
Let's, uh, not get in the way.

63
00:04:46,742 --> 00:04:48,952
{\an8}I don't understand.
You don't want the case?

64
00:04:50,996 --> 00:04:52,039
So what are you doing?

65
00:04:53,040 --> 00:04:54,124
{\an8}Nothing.

66
00:04:55,167 --> 00:04:57,044
{\an8}Why don't we just skip the part
where you lie to me

67
00:04:57,169 --> 00:04:59,505
and get right to the part where you
tell me what you're gonna do?

68
00:05:00,589 --> 00:05:02,883
{\an8}Red John let Kristina make
a call that could be traced.

69
00:05:03,008 --> 00:05:05,260
{\an8}- He's playing a game.
- With who?

70
00:05:08,806 --> 00:05:09,973
See you later.

71
00:05:13,602 --> 00:05:15,604
{\an8}Yeah, that sounds great.
I can make it there by 7:00.

72
00:05:15,896 --> 00:05:17,689
{\an8}Listen, I have to go.
I'll speak to you later, okay? Bye.

73
00:05:18,774 --> 00:05:20,359
{\an8}If you're seeing traffic
on the 50 tonight

74
00:05:20,484 --> 00:05:22,194
{\an8}you think she could set
her alarm a little earlier?

75
00:05:22,986 --> 00:05:24,905
{\an8}Okay, look, I get it.
This is, uh...

76
00:05:25,405 --> 00:05:27,866
{\an8}it's the last time you have
to hear about my love life.

77
00:05:28,700 --> 00:05:31,578
I don't care about your love life.
Just don't let it affect the job.

78
00:05:31,912 --> 00:05:33,163
{\an8}- My love life is not gonna affect--
- "Hey."

79
00:05:33,288 --> 00:05:35,415
{\an8}- Hey, boss.
- Anything on the girl in the river?

80
00:05:35,791 --> 00:05:37,084
"Name's Celia Jovanovich."

81
00:05:37,292 --> 00:05:39,503
{\an8}Some convictions for narcotics
possession. No family.

82
00:05:39,920 --> 00:05:41,004
What about the rehab angle?

83
00:05:41,129 --> 00:05:42,589
No mention of a program
in her record.

84
00:05:42,881 --> 00:05:44,091
{\an8}Well, she must've cleaned up somehow.

85
00:05:44,216 --> 00:05:47,344
{\an8}- No arrests in almost two years.
- Hey, that tattoo on our vic--

86
00:05:47,469 --> 00:05:50,180
{\an8}- it's worn by members of Visualize.
- Visualize? The cult?

87
00:05:50,722 --> 00:05:52,641
{\an8}They do work with addicts.
She could've cleaned up there.

88
00:05:53,267 --> 00:05:55,394
- See? The wings form a "v" for "Visualize".
- Yeah.

89
00:05:55,727 --> 00:05:57,020
What was the name
of the guy who runs it?

90
00:05:57,729 --> 00:06:00,524
Stiles. Bret Stiles.

91
00:06:04,319 --> 00:06:06,905
Agent Lisbon,
I'm Brother Steven Wench.

92
00:06:07,322 --> 00:06:08,615
- Mr. Jane...
- Mm.

93
00:06:08,824 --> 00:06:11,410
This is Warner Vander Hoek
our Chief of Security.

94
00:06:11,618 --> 00:06:13,662
- Julius Coles, our attorney.
- How do you do, agent?

95
00:06:13,912 --> 00:06:16,415
Quite an impressive file
at CBI, Lisbon.

96
00:06:16,623 --> 00:06:19,668
I know if anyone can find
Celia's killer, you can.

97
00:06:20,210 --> 00:06:22,671
I appreciate your confidence
Mr. Vander Hoek.

98
00:06:23,297 --> 00:06:24,548
How did you read my file?

99
00:06:24,798 --> 00:06:26,967
I spent 11 years
working Seattle Homicide.

100
00:06:27,467 --> 00:06:29,136
Seven years
in the Intelligence Division.

101
00:06:29,636 --> 00:06:32,180
Ooh. That's a whole lotta cop
for a self-help group.

102
00:06:32,806 --> 00:06:33,932
And we have enemies.

103
00:06:35,183 --> 00:06:37,060
As Mr. Stiles says...

104
00:06:37,603 --> 00:06:39,646
"The truth always does."

105
00:06:40,439 --> 00:06:41,982
Where is, uh, Bret?

106
00:06:42,816 --> 00:06:44,943
I'm afraid brother Stiles is busy

107
00:06:45,193 --> 00:06:46,445
with church business
at the moment.

108
00:06:46,570 --> 00:06:49,907
- And why are you so afraid?
- It's a figure of speech...

109
00:06:50,032 --> 00:06:54,620
- Yes, it is. Shall we? Lead the way.
- Yes, we should.

110
00:06:54,912 --> 00:06:56,914
"My name is Celia Jovanovich."

111
00:06:57,664 --> 00:07:00,208
"This picture was taken
when I had been a heroin addict"

112
00:07:00,334 --> 00:07:01,752
"for nine years."

113
00:07:02,294 --> 00:07:04,296
"I had no job or home"

114
00:07:04,963 --> 00:07:07,382
"no future, no hope."

115
00:07:08,634 --> 00:07:11,428
"But I beat addiction
and changed my life"

116
00:07:11,929 --> 00:07:14,389
"when I began to Visualize."

117
00:07:15,641 --> 00:07:18,644
Our addiction counselors found her
literally living in the streets.

118
00:07:19,102 --> 00:07:21,271
She attempted suicide three times.
They...

119
00:07:21,939 --> 00:07:23,482
They brought her here, and...

120
00:07:25,150 --> 00:07:26,193
This is what she became.

121
00:07:26,318 --> 00:07:28,528
Well, she certainly became better
at doing her makeup.

122
00:07:28,987 --> 00:07:31,740
Your low personal opinion
of Visualize is duly noted...

123
00:07:32,157 --> 00:07:35,035
But irrelevant. Let's try and confine
our discussion to the facts.

124
00:07:35,410 --> 00:07:38,330
Of course. Uh, Mr. Coles,
you're not a member here, are you?

125
00:07:38,622 --> 00:07:39,665
I am not.

126
00:07:40,207 --> 00:07:42,417
That's interesting
that Mr. Stiles would hire a lawyer

127
00:07:42,542 --> 00:07:46,213
- outside of the sacred fold. Hmm?
- Oh, what did Celia do here?

128
00:07:46,630 --> 00:07:48,048
She worked in our security section.

129
00:07:48,256 --> 00:07:49,299
It's called vigilance.

130
00:07:49,800 --> 00:07:52,552
We provide personal security
for the church's senior leaders.

131
00:07:52,886 --> 00:07:55,347
- I was her, uh, supervisor.
- What's her home address?

132
00:07:56,056 --> 00:07:59,059
She lived here. We provide homes
for members who want them.

133
00:07:59,726 --> 00:08:00,852
Celia had had it tough.

134
00:08:01,478 --> 00:08:02,854
The--the church was her haven.

135
00:08:03,647 --> 00:08:05,315
And we're gonna need to speak
to all of her friends

136
00:08:05,440 --> 00:08:07,567
- acquaintances, coworkers.
- That'll be fine

137
00:08:07,776 --> 00:08:10,946
with the proviso that I or one of my
associates be present at all times.

138
00:08:11,571 --> 00:08:13,532
Was there anybody in particular
that she was close to?

139
00:08:13,991 --> 00:08:16,201
There was a fiancé, David Herren.

140
00:08:16,618 --> 00:08:18,870
He's a member of the church
but I don't know where he is right now.

141
00:08:19,162 --> 00:08:20,205
Huh.

142
00:08:22,708 --> 00:08:24,960
I'm sure you'll be able
to locate him for us.

143
00:08:25,794 --> 00:08:28,422
Agent, I assume you will be looking
at suspects outside the church.

144
00:08:28,547 --> 00:08:30,757
I'd hate to think that this was
some sort of witch hunt.

145
00:08:31,174 --> 00:08:33,510
Oh, we'll go wherever
the investigation leads us.

146
00:08:34,636 --> 00:08:37,597
- So, um, thank you very much.
- Okay.

147
00:08:37,889 --> 00:08:38,932
Uh, excuse me.

148
00:08:40,350 --> 00:08:42,894
- Tec, interesting name.
- Yeah.

149
00:08:43,186 --> 00:08:44,563
You look like an honest young man.

150
00:08:44,813 --> 00:08:46,523
Do you know where Brother Stiles
is right now?

151
00:08:46,898 --> 00:08:48,775
- No, sir, I don't.
- Very honest.

152
00:08:49,026 --> 00:08:50,736
Terrible liar. Is--is he this way?

153
00:08:51,361 --> 00:08:52,529
Or is he this way?

154
00:08:53,113 --> 00:08:56,700
- Okay.
- Sir, I-I don't think that--uh, sir?

155
00:08:56,825 --> 00:08:59,286
- Yeah, spit it out.
- I-I don't understand what you're doing.

156
00:08:59,411 --> 00:09:00,662
You don't wanna tell me
where Stiles is

157
00:09:00,787 --> 00:09:02,873
so when I move you in his location,
you react negatively.

158
00:09:02,998 --> 00:09:04,332
I'm just reading
your negative reaction.

159
00:09:04,458 --> 00:09:06,251
Well, please stop.
You're gonna get me in trouble.

160
00:09:06,376 --> 00:09:07,419
This way?

161
00:09:12,632 --> 00:09:14,217
Please don't go in there, sir.

162
00:09:15,010 --> 00:09:16,053
Thank you.

163
00:09:20,891 --> 00:09:23,935
"You see
if the mind is free"

164
00:09:24,686 --> 00:09:27,564
"there's nothing
that you can't achieve."

165
00:09:28,065 --> 00:09:31,193
"Because then the mind
has no limits."

166
00:09:31,568 --> 00:09:35,280
It's a spaceship
with the power to travel across

167
00:09:35,447 --> 00:09:37,991
all six dimensions.

168
00:09:38,450 --> 00:09:40,827
- Journeying off to--
- Excuse me, uh, Bret?

169
00:09:41,661 --> 00:09:43,413
- I have a question.
- What?

170
00:09:44,331 --> 00:09:45,540
Sorry. Did somebody speak?

171
00:09:45,874 --> 00:09:47,876
Uh, it--it was me.

172
00:09:50,170 --> 00:09:51,421
- Patrick?
- Yeah.

173
00:09:51,671 --> 00:09:53,381
How nice to see you.

174
00:09:54,132 --> 00:09:55,801
Why offer only six dimensions?

175
00:09:56,093 --> 00:09:59,513
Is--is it to hold off a couple
of dimensions to sell later?

176
00:10:01,598 --> 00:10:03,934
I think six is quite enough.

177
00:10:04,476 --> 00:10:06,353
When did you last see
Celia Jovanovich?

178
00:10:06,853 --> 00:10:11,566
Oh, uh, Celia.
Yes, um, let me think. Um...

179
00:10:12,651 --> 00:10:15,112
I believe she worked
a security detail for me

180
00:10:15,237 --> 00:10:16,321
earlier in the week--

181
00:10:17,197 --> 00:10:20,117
a seminar for pre-members
at the Hyatt.

182
00:10:20,408 --> 00:10:21,451
Pre-members?

183
00:10:21,785 --> 00:10:24,579
Those that have not yet seen
the truth.

184
00:10:25,956 --> 00:10:27,707
You would be a pre-member.

185
00:10:28,542 --> 00:10:30,836
Poor Celia.
It's tragic, uh...

186
00:10:31,461 --> 00:10:33,964
She fought so hard
for her sobriety.

187
00:10:34,381 --> 00:10:35,924
When did you learn
of her death?

188
00:10:36,299 --> 00:10:37,467
Well, I don't know.

189
00:10:37,592 --> 00:10:39,594
I suppose
when they identified the body.

190
00:10:39,719 --> 00:10:42,347
You know, many policemen
are Visualize members.

191
00:10:43,473 --> 00:10:45,225
What do you think
happened to her?

192
00:10:45,851 --> 00:10:47,519
No idea.
You have a theory?

193
00:10:48,145 --> 00:10:49,187
Oh, no.

194
00:10:49,604 --> 00:10:51,398
I never theorize.

195
00:10:52,524 --> 00:10:55,652
We gurus must always
speak the truth

196
00:10:56,278 --> 00:10:58,113
or... nothing.

197
00:10:58,697 --> 00:11:01,449
You were surprised I was here about Celia.
Why did you think I was here?

198
00:11:02,909 --> 00:11:04,411
Kristina Frye, of course.

199
00:11:13,543 --> 00:11:14,586
Kristina Frye?

200
00:11:16,337 --> 00:11:18,089
Red John has her, right?

201
00:11:20,008 --> 00:11:21,467
It's a terrible thing.

202
00:11:23,928 --> 00:11:25,847
First, your wife and child

203
00:11:26,306 --> 00:11:27,807
now miss Frye.

204
00:11:29,684 --> 00:11:31,853
Sounds like he's jealous, Patrick.

205
00:11:32,604 --> 00:11:33,646
It sounds like...

206
00:11:34,314 --> 00:11:37,775
he wants to take away everything
and everyone that you care about.

207
00:11:39,319 --> 00:11:41,362
It's a form of love
you know.

208
00:11:45,700 --> 00:11:48,119
What do you know
about Kristina Frye and Red John?

209
00:11:51,080 --> 00:11:53,625
Patrick, I like you.

210
00:11:54,375 --> 00:11:56,252
I like your vim.

211
00:11:56,961 --> 00:11:58,379
And Red John--

212
00:11:58,922 --> 00:12:03,218
he seems to be a perfectly
unpleasant sort of fellow.

213
00:12:04,385 --> 00:12:08,306
If I knew how to get you even
half a step closer to him

214
00:12:09,349 --> 00:12:11,684
I would cross desert wastes
to tell you.

215
00:12:12,977 --> 00:12:14,520
But I don't know.

216
00:12:16,606 --> 00:12:17,649
"Avanti."

217
00:12:17,899 --> 00:12:21,236
Ah, Starsky and Hutch.
Thank goodness.

218
00:12:21,986 --> 00:12:25,531
Mr. Jane might have cut me
into small cubes by now.

219
00:12:31,621 --> 00:12:33,873
"God is in your mind
right here."

220
00:12:34,499 --> 00:12:37,293
All you have to do to see him
is clear out the bad energy.

221
00:12:37,961 --> 00:12:39,003
I'll repeat the question.

222
00:12:39,587 --> 00:12:41,965
Have you seen Celia Jovanovich
in the past 48 hours?

223
00:12:42,465 --> 00:12:44,509
I've been visiting my mother
in Chino.

224
00:12:45,176 --> 00:12:46,469
I got back this morning.

225
00:12:46,594 --> 00:12:48,012
- That's all I need. Thanks.
- Aren't you interested

226
00:12:48,137 --> 00:12:50,974
in the path to spiritual clarity
and personal freedom?

227
00:12:51,516 --> 00:12:52,558
No.

228
00:12:55,645 --> 00:12:56,688
How's it goin'?

229
00:12:57,397 --> 00:12:59,148
Well, Celia was nice
and a good team member

230
00:12:59,274 --> 00:13:01,651
and joining Visualize is a good idea.
That's it, pretty much.

231
00:13:01,901 --> 00:13:04,570
- Keep trying. You've seen Jane?
- Yeah, he's upstairs.

232
00:13:04,696 --> 00:13:06,322
Vander Hoek took him there
to see Celia's room.

233
00:13:06,698 --> 00:13:08,908
- Is he okay?
- I guess. Why?

234
00:13:09,409 --> 00:13:11,828
Nothing. Stiles just seems
to get to him a little bit.

235
00:13:12,161 --> 00:13:13,830
- That's a neat trick.
- Yeah, I wish he'd teach it to me.

236
00:13:14,122 --> 00:13:15,248
I got the fiancé's details.

237
00:13:15,373 --> 00:13:17,500
David Herren works
at a restaurant downtown.

238
00:13:18,251 --> 00:13:19,585
- Go talk to him.
- Okay.

239
00:13:20,545 --> 00:13:21,713
You--come on. Let's talk.

240
00:13:22,714 --> 00:13:26,592
Before we do, can I just ask
are you happy in your lives?

241
00:13:30,138 --> 00:13:31,180
Sit down.

242
00:13:34,684 --> 00:13:35,935
This was Celia's room.

243
00:13:38,604 --> 00:13:39,647
Thank you.

244
00:14:14,640 --> 00:14:15,683
David Herren?

245
00:14:15,892 --> 00:14:17,602
- Yeah.
- Wayne Rigsby, CBI.

246
00:14:18,144 --> 00:14:19,479
I need to, uh, talk to you
about Celia Jovanovich.

247
00:14:19,604 --> 00:14:22,190
- Yeah, yeah. Listen, the thing is I--
- "One moment, David."

248
00:14:22,648 --> 00:14:24,776
Hi. I'm Julius Coles
David's attorney.

249
00:14:25,151 --> 00:14:27,111
Wow. You guys are organized.

250
00:14:27,528 --> 00:14:28,905
"Us guys"? Feels prejudicial.

251
00:14:29,030 --> 00:14:30,323
You have a problem
with constitutional rights?

252
00:14:30,531 --> 00:14:31,574
No, sir.

253
00:14:31,866 --> 00:14:33,785
I was a mess
when I heard the news.

254
00:14:34,243 --> 00:14:35,745
But I remember
what Mr. Stiles says--

255
00:14:36,079 --> 00:14:38,456
"Clarify the mind with discipline,
order, work."

256
00:14:38,623 --> 00:14:39,665
Are you the Head Chef?

257
00:14:40,249 --> 00:14:42,752
Prep chef now.
Maybe more than that someday.

258
00:14:43,294 --> 00:14:44,879
How long had you been
engaged to Celia?

259
00:14:45,505 --> 00:14:46,547
A couple of weeks.

260
00:14:46,923 --> 00:14:48,216
And how long had you
known her before?

261
00:14:48,841 --> 00:14:52,011
- I didn't... know her. I mean--
- I don't understand.

262
00:14:53,137 --> 00:14:54,764
I had never seen her before.

263
00:14:55,181 --> 00:14:56,265
High level Visualize members

264
00:14:56,391 --> 00:14:58,393
often opt for what are called
designed marriages.

265
00:14:58,518 --> 00:15:01,646
- The partners are matched for, uh...
- Energy consilience.

266
00:15:02,105 --> 00:15:04,690
- So it was an arranged marriage?
- A rational marriage.

267
00:15:05,316 --> 00:15:07,485
I knew the minute I saw Celia
we belonged together.

268
00:15:08,111 --> 00:15:10,405
Was there someone else?
Someone angry about being replaced?

269
00:15:10,530 --> 00:15:11,614
An ex-boyfriend perhaps?

270
00:15:12,281 --> 00:15:13,324
Absolutely not.

271
00:15:13,449 --> 00:15:15,284
How can you be so certain?
You only just met her.

272
00:15:16,035 --> 00:15:18,746
Knowledge comes to those
who are open to it, agent.

273
00:15:19,288 --> 00:15:20,331
I knew Celia.

274
00:15:21,374 --> 00:15:22,458
There was no one else.

275
00:15:23,042 --> 00:15:25,795
Are you sure?
Because Celia was strangled.

276
00:15:26,254 --> 00:15:29,173
That's a killer who's upset
really wants to hurt the victim.

277
00:15:29,590 --> 00:15:31,759
There wasn't anybody who
might've been mad at you and Celia?

278
00:15:32,260 --> 00:15:34,679
- Might've made you mad?
- There's no need to answer that.

279
00:15:35,054 --> 00:15:36,097
I'm just trying to get
the picture here.

280
00:15:36,222 --> 00:15:37,849
No, you're poking at him
with wild conjecture

281
00:15:37,974 --> 00:15:39,434
to see how he reacts
and I won't have it.

282
00:15:39,809 --> 00:15:40,852
This is over.

283
00:16:28,649 --> 00:16:31,027
So I checked into Herren.
Cooking's just a hobby.

284
00:16:31,152 --> 00:16:33,237
His family's loaded--
old lumber money.

285
00:16:33,613 --> 00:16:36,032
When he turns 27
he inherits 10 million.

286
00:16:36,657 --> 00:16:38,409
That's probably why Stiles
arranged the marriage.

287
00:16:38,534 --> 00:16:42,038
With Celia married to Herren, the church
is more likely to tap into the money.

288
00:16:42,371 --> 00:16:44,123
Yeah, but it's not motive
for Herren to kill Celia.

289
00:16:44,540 --> 00:16:46,584
Oh, was there anything else
from the interviews at Visualize?

290
00:16:46,876 --> 00:16:47,919
Nothing useful.

291
00:16:48,503 --> 00:16:51,339
They all seem so happy.
I mean, truly happy.

292
00:16:51,923 --> 00:16:53,466
Yeah. It's creepy.

293
00:16:54,425 --> 00:16:56,886
Jane. Kinda lost track of you
at Visualize.

294
00:16:57,762 --> 00:16:58,804
Took a nap.

295
00:17:02,016 --> 00:17:03,142
Is something on your mind?

296
00:17:03,893 --> 00:17:05,937
No, no.
Um, I'm gonna be upstairs.

297
00:17:10,191 --> 00:17:13,027
Celia had some problems
with Visualize philosophy--

298
00:17:13,402 --> 00:17:15,029
questions, issues with the dogma.

299
00:17:15,154 --> 00:17:17,865
She, uh, might've wanted
to talk to someone about it.

300
00:17:18,282 --> 00:17:19,700
Someone outside of the church.

301
00:17:24,121 --> 00:17:27,041
Someone mentioned a friend
of hers who was a member but left.

302
00:17:27,667 --> 00:17:29,669
Um... Lucy Joel.

303
00:17:33,589 --> 00:17:36,217
Are you sure nobody was following you,
saw you come in?

304
00:17:36,342 --> 00:17:37,843
Lucy, nobody followed us.

305
00:17:38,469 --> 00:17:39,804
I'm not crazy, okay?

306
00:17:40,596 --> 00:17:42,723
I have been followed
and threatened.

307
00:17:43,724 --> 00:17:45,977
Visualize doesn't like
when people leave the hive.

308
00:17:47,103 --> 00:17:49,730
When you're a member
every week you sit down in front of a camera

309
00:17:49,855 --> 00:17:51,774
and lay out every bad thing
you've done.

310
00:17:54,443 --> 00:17:56,112
I mean, everything.

311
00:17:56,737 --> 00:17:57,863
It's called ventilation.

312
00:17:58,281 --> 00:18:01,242
Your vent vids.
It's supposed to air you out.

313
00:18:01,826 --> 00:18:03,911
It makes you feel great, clean.

314
00:18:05,830 --> 00:18:07,707
Then when you're leaving
they say, "Whoa."

315
00:18:08,374 --> 00:18:10,042
"We know all this nasty stuff."

316
00:18:10,710 --> 00:18:12,670
You're not gonna say anything
bad about Visualize, are you?

317
00:18:12,837 --> 00:18:14,422
We're not here to get dirt
on Visualize.

318
00:18:15,047 --> 00:18:16,340
We wanna talk about Celia.

319
00:18:17,300 --> 00:18:18,342
Yeah.

320
00:18:19,760 --> 00:18:20,803
She was sweet

321
00:18:21,178 --> 00:18:22,513
almost too nice, you know?

322
00:18:23,973 --> 00:18:25,683
She needed people
a little too much.

323
00:18:27,768 --> 00:18:29,145
She knew Visualize was crazy

324
00:18:29,729 --> 00:18:31,147
but they'd gotten her clean.

325
00:18:33,566 --> 00:18:35,151
And she was scared
to leave, you know?

326
00:18:36,319 --> 00:18:38,404
Thought she'd start using again.

327
00:18:39,155 --> 00:18:40,197
Was she in touch with you?

328
00:18:41,240 --> 00:18:43,409
She'd call, just to talk

329
00:18:44,076 --> 00:18:46,329
bitch about the church
you know, stuff.

330
00:18:46,621 --> 00:18:48,039
Was there anything specific
on her mind?

331
00:18:49,915 --> 00:18:51,083
I-I can't. I'm sorry.

332
00:18:51,208 --> 00:18:52,752
- Lucy, listen. We can offer you--
- I don't want any trouble. No...

333
00:18:52,877 --> 00:18:54,879
It was really hard to leave that place.

334
00:18:56,005 --> 00:18:58,549
Now I'm good with the church
and the church is good with me.

335
00:18:59,467 --> 00:19:00,551
Everything's good.

336
00:19:02,345 --> 00:19:03,596
Listen, I know you're scared

337
00:19:04,680 --> 00:19:06,349
but right now
you're Celia's guardian

338
00:19:07,141 --> 00:19:08,392
the only one that can help her.

339
00:19:09,310 --> 00:19:10,353
It's up to you.

340
00:19:15,524 --> 00:19:18,277
She was having an affair with
somebody very big in the church.

341
00:19:18,819 --> 00:19:20,196
She wouldn't tell me his name.

342
00:19:21,238 --> 00:19:22,990
Then she was supposed
to marry Herren.

343
00:19:24,075 --> 00:19:26,744
And he was sweet
kept saying he loved her.

344
00:19:28,079 --> 00:19:29,538
She felt bad lying to him.

345
00:19:31,707 --> 00:19:32,792
Last time I talked to her

346
00:19:33,084 --> 00:19:34,627
she said
she had to do something

347
00:19:35,086 --> 00:19:36,295
but she didn't say what.

348
00:19:39,006 --> 00:19:41,050
And if anybody finds out
I told you that

349
00:19:42,718 --> 00:19:44,053
I am so dead.

350
00:19:50,101 --> 00:19:52,603
You were great in there.
"You're Celia's guardian."

351
00:19:52,937 --> 00:19:53,979
It was nice.

352
00:19:56,899 --> 00:19:57,983
I lied this morning.

353
00:19:59,902 --> 00:20:01,529
I do care that you're seeing
someone else.

354
00:20:02,071 --> 00:20:03,114
It hurts a little.

355
00:20:04,699 --> 00:20:07,076
I mean, it's no biggie.
I'll get over it.

356
00:20:08,160 --> 00:20:09,495
I want us to be friends.

357
00:20:11,831 --> 00:20:13,165
We can get to that point, right?

358
00:20:14,834 --> 00:20:16,085
Can we be just friends?

359
00:20:17,128 --> 00:20:18,754
Yeah. Sure, we can.

360
00:20:19,964 --> 00:20:22,007
Good. I'd like that.

361
00:20:26,804 --> 00:20:27,847
Behind us.

362
00:20:28,097 --> 00:20:30,474
- Huh?
- Someone's tailing us.

363
00:20:32,435 --> 00:20:33,936
- Visualize?
- Oh, yeah.

364
00:20:35,104 --> 00:20:36,313
I guess Lucy isn't crazy.

365
00:20:37,022 --> 00:20:38,107
Getting the plates.

366
00:20:39,650 --> 00:20:41,694
- Should I pull 'em over?
- Can you get behind 'em?

367
00:20:42,778 --> 00:20:45,489
Throw a loop? Easy. Watch.

368
00:20:48,743 --> 00:20:49,785
Grace!

369
00:20:55,875 --> 00:20:56,959
Grace!

370
00:21:01,005 --> 00:21:03,466
- You okay? You okay?
- Yeah, yeah. You?

371
00:21:03,716 --> 00:21:05,301
- Yeah.
- I just--I just need a minute.

372
00:21:05,426 --> 00:21:06,969
Go see the other guys.

373
00:21:13,726 --> 00:21:17,146
Hey. CBI. You wanna tell me
what the hell you're doing?

374
00:21:17,730 --> 00:21:20,065
FBI. I could ask you
the same thing.

375
00:21:27,905 --> 00:21:30,616
- Agent O'Laughlin, is it?
- Craig O'Laughlin.

376
00:21:30,949 --> 00:21:31,992
That's right, ma'am.

377
00:21:32,117 --> 00:21:35,162
You wanna tell me why the FBI
was tailing two of my agents?

378
00:21:35,579 --> 00:21:36,622
Sure.

379
00:21:36,789 --> 00:21:39,708
We've been looking at Bret Stiles
and Visualize for a couple years now.

380
00:21:40,042 --> 00:21:43,420
And we've had allegations of tax fraud,
racketeering and a lot worse

381
00:21:43,545 --> 00:21:45,172
but we haven't gotten our hands
on anybody that could tell us

382
00:21:45,297 --> 00:21:47,549
about the organization.
Tight as a drum.

383
00:21:47,716 --> 00:21:48,967
Yeah, but why follow us?

384
00:21:49,343 --> 00:21:52,012
My boss thinks Stiles may have people
inside law enforcement

385
00:21:52,137 --> 00:21:55,224
which would explain why we're not
getting anywhere with the investigation.

386
00:21:55,849 --> 00:21:58,101
Y-you think that we're working
with Visualize?

387
00:21:58,268 --> 00:22:00,687
She wanted us to look
into the possibility. That's all.

388
00:22:01,146 --> 00:22:02,606
And I've seen no evidence of it.

389
00:22:04,858 --> 00:22:06,360
What you did was reckless.

390
00:22:06,568 --> 00:22:08,779
I should bring you up
for departmental discipline.

391
00:22:09,112 --> 00:22:11,907
But he shouldn't have been following you
so I'm gonna let it pass.

392
00:22:14,117 --> 00:22:17,079
And you tell your boss
if she wants to catch bad guys

393
00:22:17,246 --> 00:22:18,789
she should follow bad guys.

394
00:22:21,041 --> 00:22:22,709
It was a pleasure working
with the FBI.

395
00:22:25,712 --> 00:22:27,840
Hey, listen. I'm sorry about that.

396
00:22:28,382 --> 00:22:29,424
Does it hurt?

397
00:22:30,133 --> 00:22:32,636
No. No, it's not that bad.
Thanks.

398
00:22:34,179 --> 00:22:37,182
You know, Van Pelt...

399
00:22:38,767 --> 00:22:40,769
You--you related
to Amos Van Pelt, by any chance?

400
00:22:40,936 --> 00:22:42,437
The football coach at Burton?

401
00:22:42,980 --> 00:22:44,064
He's my father.

402
00:22:45,357 --> 00:22:47,943
Whoa. Uh, he's one hell of a coach.

403
00:22:48,485 --> 00:22:50,153
I was a wide receiver
at U. of M.

404
00:22:50,320 --> 00:22:52,406
Your, uh, your dad gave us
one tough game.

405
00:22:53,824 --> 00:22:54,867
O'Laughlin...

406
00:22:55,284 --> 00:22:57,160
Didn't you go NFL?
Tennessee.

407
00:22:57,911 --> 00:22:59,997
I did, yeah.
Yeah, just a couple of years.

408
00:23:00,455 --> 00:23:01,665
Thanks for remembering.

409
00:23:02,583 --> 00:23:05,419
Anyway, I should get back to the office
get beat up by my own boss.

410
00:23:06,712 --> 00:23:09,548
You see your dad
tell him he's remembered.

411
00:23:10,757 --> 00:23:12,134
I will. Thanks.

412
00:23:12,885 --> 00:23:13,927
Yeah.

413
00:23:18,765 --> 00:23:19,808
Hey. Excuse me.

414
00:23:21,935 --> 00:23:23,228
You're the FBI guy, right?

415
00:23:23,812 --> 00:23:25,439
I'm a special agent in charge
if that's what you mean.

416
00:23:25,564 --> 00:23:26,773
Now, that's exactly
what I mean.

417
00:23:26,899 --> 00:23:28,609
So you guys are
investigating Visualize

418
00:23:28,734 --> 00:23:30,360
and this character
Bret Stiles, right?

419
00:23:31,445 --> 00:23:33,113
I guess that's common
knowledge by now.

420
00:23:34,197 --> 00:23:36,742
Yeah. Do you have a guy
deep inside the church?

421
00:23:36,867 --> 00:23:38,410
You know, un-undercover agent?

422
00:23:38,619 --> 00:23:40,329
You can't seriously
be asking me that.

423
00:23:40,996 --> 00:23:43,248
So that's a "yes".
Any chance of a name?

424
00:23:44,291 --> 00:23:46,001
No. No chance.

425
00:23:48,378 --> 00:23:49,838
We have to get back
to Visualize.

426
00:23:50,380 --> 00:23:51,423
Why is that?

427
00:23:51,715 --> 00:23:54,468
Celia Jovanovich was almost
certainly killed by her lover

428
00:23:54,593 --> 00:23:57,304
so she almost certainly
mentioned his name

429
00:23:57,429 --> 00:23:58,472
in her vent video.

430
00:23:58,680 --> 00:24:00,515
Ergo, we need
to see her videos.

431
00:24:01,266 --> 00:24:02,351
I'll get my coat.

432
00:24:05,354 --> 00:24:06,396
What do you have in there?

433
00:24:09,107 --> 00:24:10,943
Oh, look at that.
Thank you.

434
00:24:13,195 --> 00:24:15,322
"To make ourselves
fully conscious"

435
00:24:16,073 --> 00:24:19,201
"the challenge is
to expand the power of mind"

436
00:24:19,743 --> 00:24:24,289
"by dispelling doubt and guilt
so that we may find in our--"

437
00:24:25,999 --> 00:24:28,126
Sorry. Didn't mean
to startle anyone.

438
00:24:29,419 --> 00:24:31,463
Well, actually, I did.
You got a minute?

439
00:24:32,798 --> 00:24:34,091
What is it, Mr. Jane?

440
00:24:37,886 --> 00:24:39,680
You're the FBI's
undercover agent, right?

441
00:24:39,972 --> 00:24:41,765
- What?
- I need a favor.

442
00:24:42,224 --> 00:24:44,101
Just a small one.
Get rid of 'em.

443
00:24:47,020 --> 00:24:48,063
Guys, take a break.

444
00:24:55,696 --> 00:24:57,489
I have no idea
what you're talking about.

445
00:24:57,990 --> 00:25:00,283
Well, when I just popped
the bag right now

446
00:25:01,034 --> 00:25:02,244
your hand went for your hip.

447
00:25:02,577 --> 00:25:04,871
Like you were reaching for your gun.
It's a cop instinct.

448
00:25:05,080 --> 00:25:06,123
Never goes away.

449
00:25:10,210 --> 00:25:11,712
Do you have any idea
what you're doing?

450
00:25:12,170 --> 00:25:13,630
This is an ongoing investigation

451
00:25:13,755 --> 00:25:16,717
and I spent three years working
my way into this organization.

452
00:25:16,842 --> 00:25:19,594
Hey, don't freak out, Serpico.
I need one little thing.

453
00:25:20,846 --> 00:25:21,888
Forget it.

454
00:25:22,347 --> 00:25:23,390
Your investigation is dead.

455
00:25:23,515 --> 00:25:25,934
If I picked you out, then Stiles
has definitely picked you out.

456
00:25:26,101 --> 00:25:27,436
The only reason

457
00:25:27,769 --> 00:25:29,938
he hasn't gotten rid of you
is because he's using you.

458
00:25:30,063 --> 00:25:32,024
He's feeding you false information.

459
00:25:32,899 --> 00:25:34,192
Do you have any usable evidence?

460
00:25:35,777 --> 00:25:38,280
No. Didn't think so.
And you never will.

461
00:25:39,364 --> 00:25:40,407
You can help me, though.

462
00:25:40,615 --> 00:25:43,076
Together, we can catch
Celia Jovanovich's killer.

463
00:25:44,578 --> 00:25:45,620
What's this about?

464
00:25:46,329 --> 00:25:48,081
I need to see
one of her vent videos

465
00:25:48,206 --> 00:25:50,125
and I need you to take me
to where they're kept.

466
00:25:50,500 --> 00:25:52,419
- Get a warrant.
- Warrants take time.

467
00:25:52,544 --> 00:25:55,505
And meanwhile, back at the ranch
they're wiping the tapes.

468
00:25:59,426 --> 00:26:04,014
The room where they're stored
is full of security cameras.

469
00:26:05,015 --> 00:26:07,559
- They'll be on to you in minutes.
- Yes, they will.

470
00:26:09,352 --> 00:26:10,687
That's what I'm talking about.

471
00:26:11,813 --> 00:26:12,856
Let's go.

472
00:26:20,197 --> 00:26:21,573
Ah, Agent Lisbon.

473
00:26:21,907 --> 00:26:24,785
What's all this about you wanting
Celia's vent videos?

474
00:26:24,910 --> 00:26:26,453
We believe Celia Jovanovich

475
00:26:26,578 --> 00:26:28,622
may have identified her killer
in one of the videos.

476
00:26:28,747 --> 00:26:31,541
- We'd like to take a look at 'em.
- No, no, no. That's impossible.

477
00:26:31,958 --> 00:26:35,212
The ventilations show our members
at their most vulnerable.

478
00:26:35,420 --> 00:26:37,964
Only senior members of the church
are allowed to see them.

479
00:26:38,256 --> 00:26:40,383
I mean
I could no more show you them

480
00:26:40,675 --> 00:26:42,719
than a priest could discuss
a confession.

481
00:26:44,096 --> 00:26:46,640
Now, if you'll please
excuse me...

482
00:26:47,099 --> 00:26:48,141
- Sir?
- Yeah.

483
00:26:49,059 --> 00:26:50,685
Security feed of Patrick Jane.

484
00:26:51,103 --> 00:26:52,145
What?

485
00:26:55,857 --> 00:27:00,070
Agent, this is a security camera feed
from our video room.

486
00:27:00,529 --> 00:27:02,072
What's going on?

487
00:27:15,293 --> 00:27:18,046
It's been about half an hour.
This is outrageous.

488
00:27:18,380 --> 00:27:19,422
I'm getting bored.

489
00:27:20,340 --> 00:27:23,844
Mr. Stiles is calling in every
important person he knows

490
00:27:23,969 --> 00:27:25,387
to try and get us fired.

491
00:27:26,138 --> 00:27:27,305
It takes time.

492
00:27:32,936 --> 00:27:34,771
You're done.
You are done.

493
00:27:34,896 --> 00:27:35,939
We've spoken to your superiors

494
00:27:36,064 --> 00:27:37,774
explained to them
that we view Mr. Jane's actions

495
00:27:37,899 --> 00:27:39,609
as a grievous breach
of civil liberties.

496
00:27:39,734 --> 00:27:41,611
We'll be pursuing
civil and criminal remedies.

497
00:27:42,028 --> 00:27:43,071
Meh.

498
00:27:43,405 --> 00:27:44,447
I'm curious.

499
00:27:44,865 --> 00:27:48,410
You couldn't hope to watch
these videos for any length of time.

500
00:27:49,077 --> 00:27:51,705
What did you think you'd accomplish
by coming here?

501
00:27:52,080 --> 00:27:53,123
Oh, we'll see the videos.

502
00:27:53,790 --> 00:27:56,293
Oh, you will see them, will you?
And--and how is that?

503
00:27:56,918 --> 00:27:59,629
- You'll give them to us.
- Oh, really?

504
00:28:00,046 --> 00:28:01,464
And why? Why?

505
00:28:09,514 --> 00:28:11,683
Celia Jovanovich
was killed by her lover--

506
00:28:12,309 --> 00:28:13,727
someone very high up
in your church

507
00:28:13,852 --> 00:28:16,646
someone that is very probably
in this room right now.

508
00:28:16,980 --> 00:28:20,275
Well, that's very interesting
if it were true.

509
00:28:20,400 --> 00:28:23,403
And I daresay, is mentioned
in her videos.

510
00:28:24,154 --> 00:28:26,531
So if you say
you'll give us the videos

511
00:28:27,115 --> 00:28:28,992
the killer will identify himself.

512
00:28:29,451 --> 00:28:31,870
He will be the man
that insists most forcefully

513
00:28:31,995 --> 00:28:33,413
that you shouldn't give 'em
to us.

514
00:28:35,123 --> 00:28:37,250
- What if I killed her?
- You?

515
00:28:39,628 --> 00:28:40,837
You wouldn't hurt a fly.

516
00:28:46,176 --> 00:28:50,513
Patrick has offered a very,
um, persuasive argument.

517
00:28:50,639 --> 00:28:53,266
I'm going to be handing over
the videos to him.

518
00:28:53,516 --> 00:28:54,559
No!

519
00:28:56,811 --> 00:28:58,396
No. Absolutely n--
I-I can't allow that.

520
00:28:58,605 --> 00:28:59,648
Why not?

521
00:28:59,940 --> 00:29:01,691
The precedent
would be unacceptable.

522
00:29:01,816 --> 00:29:03,318
It would--
it would open up all manner

523
00:29:03,443 --> 00:29:04,819
of intrusive police action.

524
00:29:05,111 --> 00:29:08,365
That sounds like lawyer speak
for "I did it. I did it. I'm guilty."

525
00:29:09,324 --> 00:29:13,119
Mr. Coles, in a week or so,
forensics is gonna have processed

526
00:29:13,245 --> 00:29:15,330
the DNA that was under
the victim's fingernails.

527
00:29:15,664 --> 00:29:17,123
We're gonna need a sample
from you.

528
00:29:17,540 --> 00:29:20,043
That's ridiculous. That--
that is completely unnecessary.

529
00:29:20,168 --> 00:29:21,836
No, it's just a pinprick.
Doesn't hurt a bit.

530
00:29:22,295 --> 00:29:24,965
Julius, please.
Tell me...

531
00:29:26,049 --> 00:29:29,386
You did not kill
that young woman.

532
00:29:32,138 --> 00:29:33,848
No, I didn't.

533
00:29:36,768 --> 00:29:39,521
That one--that--that looked like
it did hurt. Huh?

534
00:29:42,899 --> 00:29:44,025
She was a sweet girl.

535
00:29:44,484 --> 00:29:46,027
I'd see her
when I came to meet Bret.

536
00:29:46,528 --> 00:29:48,530
She liked to talk about the book
she was reading.

537
00:29:49,823 --> 00:29:52,659
Things just went from there.
I-I was...

538
00:29:54,077 --> 00:29:55,537
I was very fond of her.

539
00:29:56,830 --> 00:29:58,623
And then Herren came
into the picture.

540
00:29:59,958 --> 00:30:01,793
Celia said she had
to tell Herren the truth...

541
00:30:02,168 --> 00:30:03,211
about us.

542
00:30:04,796 --> 00:30:06,715
I told her, Visualize was
my only client.

543
00:30:07,299 --> 00:30:08,466
Bret would banish me

544
00:30:08,633 --> 00:30:11,928
if he knew I-I was involved
with a member.

545
00:30:13,847 --> 00:30:15,390
She just kept saying
she couldn't lie.

546
00:30:16,891 --> 00:30:18,768
She couldn't lie
to save my career.

547
00:30:21,771 --> 00:30:22,814
I got angry.

548
00:30:23,857 --> 00:30:24,899
And we fought.

549
00:30:28,069 --> 00:30:29,112
It happened.

550
00:30:36,119 --> 00:30:37,162
So we have a deal?

551
00:30:37,912 --> 00:30:39,956
D.A. agreed--
involuntary manslaughter.

552
00:30:40,081 --> 00:30:41,541
Three years with time served.

553
00:30:41,750 --> 00:30:44,210
In exchange
for your cooperation

554
00:30:44,336 --> 00:30:48,214
with the FBI's investigation
into Visualize and Bret Stiles.

555
00:30:49,799 --> 00:30:50,842
Okay, you got it.

556
00:30:52,135 --> 00:30:53,887
I look forward to working
with you, Mr. Coles.

557
00:31:03,980 --> 00:31:06,524
Ah. Three years is nothing.

558
00:31:07,567 --> 00:31:10,153
It's the way of the world.
He's selling Stiles. He's a big fish.

559
00:31:10,278 --> 00:31:11,780
The FBI has to pay.

560
00:31:12,489 --> 00:31:14,157
If you think
about this stuff too much

561
00:31:14,282 --> 00:31:15,658
you'll drive yourself crazy.

562
00:31:16,659 --> 00:31:17,702
That's Herren.

563
00:31:19,079 --> 00:31:20,121
Gun!

564
00:31:25,001 --> 00:31:26,044
"Drop it!"

565
00:31:26,336 --> 00:31:27,379
- "Drop your gun!"
- "On the ground!"

566
00:31:27,504 --> 00:31:29,672
Drop it! Drop it now!
Get your hands above your head!

567
00:31:30,298 --> 00:31:31,341
Don't move!

568
00:31:35,804 --> 00:31:37,639
Get your head down!
Head down!

569
00:31:47,730 --> 00:31:50,274
I had to do something.
He killed my soulmate.

570
00:31:50,817 --> 00:31:52,819
Inactivity is the sign
of the clouded mind.

571
00:31:53,152 --> 00:31:56,030
- Discipline, order, work.
- Where'd you get the gun?

572
00:31:57,323 --> 00:31:58,991
I stole it from the desk
of the manager.

573
00:31:59,409 --> 00:32:01,244
He keeps it
for making night deposits.

574
00:32:01,869 --> 00:32:03,246
Did anyone else know
what you were gonna do?

575
00:32:04,580 --> 00:32:05,623
Put me in prison.

576
00:32:06,082 --> 00:32:08,209
I don't care.
My heart is free.

577
00:32:09,168 --> 00:32:10,670
The minute I saw him, I knew.

578
00:32:11,546 --> 00:32:12,588
I did the right thing.

579
00:32:13,339 --> 00:32:14,507
Did anyone else know?

580
00:32:16,217 --> 00:32:18,469
No. It was my idea.

581
00:33:07,393 --> 00:33:08,686
Thanks for your time.

582
00:33:10,855 --> 00:33:13,149
I understand Herren confessed.

583
00:33:16,027 --> 00:33:17,361
He didn't mention your name.

584
00:33:18,279 --> 00:33:19,697
The poor soul.

585
00:33:21,073 --> 00:33:24,118
But...
Why would he mention me?

586
00:33:24,952 --> 00:33:25,995
Well...

587
00:33:26,871 --> 00:33:28,289
you didn't go
and tell him to kill the man

588
00:33:28,414 --> 00:33:30,333
but you clarified his options

589
00:33:30,500 --> 00:33:33,085
which is as good as killing him
as far as I'm concerned.

590
00:33:35,004 --> 00:33:36,506
Is that the official view?

591
00:33:37,590 --> 00:33:38,716
Is this why you wanted to see me?

592
00:33:38,841 --> 00:33:40,468
'Cause a phone call
would've been fine.

593
00:33:40,968 --> 00:33:42,303
The FBI's given up.

594
00:33:42,887 --> 00:33:44,096
Oh, that's a shame.

595
00:33:44,972 --> 00:33:48,601
I rather enjoyed Brother Wench
and his clumsy machinations.

596
00:33:48,893 --> 00:33:50,061
Oh, well, there it is.

597
00:33:50,978 --> 00:33:52,021
You're safe.

598
00:33:52,647 --> 00:33:53,689
Bravo.

599
00:33:54,023 --> 00:33:57,610
Well, always nice to know
but that's not why I'm here.

600
00:33:58,569 --> 00:34:03,449
It seems that your friend John
is planning a surprise party for you.

601
00:34:07,119 --> 00:34:08,579
How do you know
what Red John is planning?

602
00:34:08,704 --> 00:34:10,748
- It doesn't matter.
- It certainly matters to me.

603
00:34:10,873 --> 00:34:12,959
How do you know
what Red John is planning?

604
00:34:14,377 --> 00:34:17,171
My dear chap
I know so much more

605
00:34:17,296 --> 00:34:20,424
than you or Red John
could ever imagine.

606
00:34:21,676 --> 00:34:25,012
Accept this as a gift from a friend. Or not.

607
00:35:11,976 --> 00:35:13,019
"Clear!"

608
00:35:13,561 --> 00:35:14,687
"Clear upstairs."

609
00:35:15,313 --> 00:35:16,689
- All clear.
- Clear.

610
00:35:17,857 --> 00:35:18,899
Boss.

611
00:35:41,005 --> 00:35:42,048
Boss.

612
00:35:54,644 --> 00:35:55,686
Kristina?

613
00:36:02,777 --> 00:36:03,819
Kristina.

614
00:36:15,581 --> 00:36:18,417
EMT said she had a puncture wound
in one arm, like from an IV.

615
00:36:18,834 --> 00:36:20,586
Must be how Red John
got the blood out of her.

616
00:36:21,128 --> 00:36:22,838
He also said there was
no other sign of assault--

617
00:36:23,005 --> 00:36:24,632
physical, sexual, anything.

618
00:36:25,132 --> 00:36:26,384
Why won't she speak?

619
00:36:27,301 --> 00:36:28,386
What did he do to her?

620
00:36:37,061 --> 00:36:39,021
Still nothing.
Not a sound.

621
00:36:40,481 --> 00:36:41,607
Okay.

622
00:36:50,991 --> 00:36:52,034
Remember this?

623
00:37:01,001 --> 00:37:02,837
Come on, Kristina.
Listen, it's Jane.

624
00:37:03,587 --> 00:37:04,714
You remember me.

625
00:37:06,716 --> 00:37:08,008
I know you do.

626
00:37:12,304 --> 00:37:14,306
What was the worst date
you ever had?

627
00:37:15,641 --> 00:37:16,684
Huh?

628
00:37:27,611 --> 00:37:28,821
Kristina, please.

629
00:37:30,156 --> 00:37:32,074
Please stop this.
Just speak to me.

630
00:37:52,970 --> 00:37:54,346
Psych personnel
are on their way.

631
00:37:57,558 --> 00:37:58,601
Could be worse, you know.

632
00:37:59,268 --> 00:38:00,311
She could be dead.

633
00:38:04,023 --> 00:38:06,358
I guess tea
is always worth a try.

634
00:38:41,101 --> 00:38:43,229
- What is he doing?
- I have no idea.

635
00:38:56,826 --> 00:38:58,786
I call on the spirits.

636
00:39:03,666 --> 00:39:07,670
I ask for the presence of the departed soul
of Kristina Frye.

637
00:39:10,840 --> 00:39:12,925
Reveal yourself
Kristina Frye.

638
00:39:14,969 --> 00:39:16,345
Can you hear me, Kristina?

639
00:39:23,269 --> 00:39:24,728
I can hear you, Patrick.

640
00:39:26,730 --> 00:39:27,773
Well, thank you.

641
00:39:28,983 --> 00:39:30,526
Thank you
for speaking with me.

642
00:39:31,610 --> 00:39:33,237
I'm so glad you called on me.

643
00:39:34,446 --> 00:39:36,407
I knew in the end
you'd become a believer.

644
00:39:37,157 --> 00:39:38,951
- I am not a believer.
- I hear sadness in your voice.

645
00:39:39,076 --> 00:39:40,411
Don't be sad, Patrick.

646
00:39:41,704 --> 00:39:42,997
Death is not the end.

647
00:39:44,832 --> 00:39:46,792
The afterlife's a beautiful place.

648
00:39:47,793 --> 00:39:49,211
It's peaceful here.

649
00:39:50,963 --> 00:39:52,006
Happy.

650
00:39:53,966 --> 00:39:55,009
You're not dead.

651
00:39:56,093 --> 00:39:59,138
You're talking to a ghost
and still you're a skeptic.

652
00:40:00,890 --> 00:40:02,433
You are impossible.

653
00:40:02,892 --> 00:40:04,810
You're not dead, Kristina.

654
00:40:05,853 --> 00:40:06,896
You're alive.

655
00:40:07,396 --> 00:40:08,606
You're in denial.

656
00:40:10,232 --> 00:40:12,026
Eventually, you'll accept the truth.

657
00:40:12,985 --> 00:40:14,278
I know it's hard.

658
00:40:16,405 --> 00:40:18,657
God knows I struggled
against it myself.

659
00:40:22,828 --> 00:40:25,748
But you can't... fight... death.

660
00:40:27,458 --> 00:40:28,500
How did you die?

661
00:40:30,127 --> 00:40:31,378
I don't remember.

662
00:40:33,297 --> 00:40:35,799
It's funny how things
become unimportant.

663
00:40:37,676 --> 00:40:39,553
It's as if my life
was a dream.

664
00:40:41,096 --> 00:40:42,139
I woke up.

665
00:40:43,098 --> 00:40:44,683
I can't recall what happened.

666
00:40:49,438 --> 00:40:50,898
Did you see Red John?

667
00:40:53,359 --> 00:40:55,152
- Who?
- Red John.

668
00:40:56,946 --> 00:40:59,615
Red John--the man
that abducted you.

669
00:41:04,244 --> 00:41:06,789
I don't understand
what you're talking about.

670
00:41:34,066 --> 00:41:35,359
Oh. Yeah. Sure.

671
00:41:41,365 --> 00:41:43,993
Apparently, Bret Stiles
is out of the country.

672
00:41:44,201 --> 00:41:46,120
He's opening a center in Jakarta.

673
00:41:46,745 --> 00:41:49,206
Visualize people say they don't know
when he'll be back.

674
00:41:50,207 --> 00:41:51,250
Figures.

675
00:41:53,252 --> 00:41:56,380
Boss. We caught one.
Downtown.

676
00:42:01,260 --> 00:42:02,302
Are you okay?

677
00:42:05,431 --> 00:42:06,849
We're up. Let's go.
